      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T08:33:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can eliminate this unsafe block:\n```rust\nmacro_rules! const_cstr {\n    ($str:literal) \u003d\u003e {{\n        const S: \u0026str \u003d concat!($str, \"\\0\");\n        const C: \u0026::core::ffi::CStr \u003d match ::core::ffi::CStr::from_bytes_with_nul(S.as_bytes()) {\n            Ok(v) \u003d\u003e v,\n            Err(_) \u003d\u003e panic!(\"string contains interior NUL\"),\n        };\n        C\n    }};\n}\n```\nSince the panic is in a const, the check is guaranteed to happen at compile time. There is no runtime cost of this.",
